evelopment headers or something else.\r\n\r\n**What you expected to happen**: It will be good if bazel build rules will validate environment and warn users about missing components.\r\n\r\n**How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**: CentOS 7 or OpenSuSE 42.x environment. Install JDK, bazel, make, gcc normally. Run `make bazel-build` and it will result in series of errors either for `missing dependency declaration for /usr/include/foo.h` (in case of g++ missing) or `/usr/bin/ld: error: cannot find -lc` ( in case of static devel files are missing)\r\n\r\n\r\n**Anything else we need to know?**:\r\ncc @ixdy \r\n\r\n**Environment**:\r\n- Kubernetes version (use `kubectl version`): master branch\r\n- Cloud provider or hardware configuration**: n/a\r\n- OS (e.g. from /etc/os-release): CentOS 7, OpenSuSE 42.3\r\n- Kernel (e.g. `uname -a`): n/a\r\n- Install tools: \r\n- Others:\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/51623/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/51623/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]